Z","body":"This seems different from how other session backends behave, for example the `cache` backend also [silently revives sessions](https://github.com/tltx/django/blob/74019e3165f069b58de9bf6d25373f66f1ba889e/django/contrib/sessions/backends/cache.py#L53-L64).\n","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/django/django/issues/comments/176862942/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/django/django/issues/comments/176869284","html_url":"https://github.com/django/django/pull/5950#issuecomment-176869284","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/django/django/issues/5950","id":176869284,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDE3Njg2OTI4NA==","user":{"login":"charettes","id":9293,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkyOTM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9293?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/charettes","html_url":"https://github.com/charettes","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charettes/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charettes/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charettes/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charettes/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charettes/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charettes/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charettes/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charettes/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charettes/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2016-01-29T17:19:04Z","updated_at":"2016-01-29T17:19:04Z","body":"I'd like to see a test added to `SessionTestsMixin` to make sure the behavior is consistent across all backends.\n\nAs to what the actual behavior should be on update failure is the actual issue here. I don't believe raising a backend specific exception is acceptable here. The only think I can think of right now is exposing an `UpdateError` class that is raised in the rare case where this rare condition happens and have `SessionMiddleware` deal with it.\n","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/django/django/issues/comments/176869284/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/django/django/issues/comments/178052147","html_url":"https://github.com/django/django/pull/5950#issuecomment-178052147","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/django/django/issues/5950","id":178052147,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDE3ODA1MjE0Nw==","user":{"login":"tltx","id":13788469,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzNzg4NDY5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/13788469?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tltx","html_url":"https://github.com/tltx","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tltx/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tltx/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tltx/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tltx/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tltx/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tltx/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tltx/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tltx/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tltx/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2016-02-01T16:20:51Z","updated_at":"2016-02-01T16:20:51Z","body":"Thanks for your feedback!\n\nThe test now run against all backends instead of just db.SessionStore. However, this bug only affects DB backends, sp